# What boot starts once the drivers are running: from the system volume,
# when / is one, or from the initramfs. A shell on the serial line, the
# first, which boot waits for, so that its exit stops the system; its
# terminal is console, which uart serves. font, the font service, owns
# the fonts and gives every program with a window its text's glyphs; it
# starts before wm, which asks it first. wm, the compositor, owns the
# screen through display and keeps windows on it for its clients. The
# system is these services only: no app is started here, so the desktop
# starts empty, and an app is started from the launcher. audio, the
# audio server, owns the sound devices its drivers attach and serves
# audio, which play, speak, rec and speech use; usb-audio after it
# attaches each USB audio device's streams, QEMU's usb-audio speaker
# with QEMU_USB=audio, or a microphone passed through. agentd, the
# agent's server, last: with no /etc/agent/config it says so and exits
# (make agent-etc makes one), and otherwise waits for its home's
# volume, /Volumes/data, and serves agent, which run agent talks to.
# speech after it: with no /Volumes/data/speech/whistle.cact, which the
# installer fetches, it says so and exits; otherwise it reads Whistle
# and says what is heard while F12 is held to the agent.
# tests/vt.sh boots tests/vt/etc/system in place of this, with two vts.
start /bin/sh
start /sbin/font
start /sbin/wm
start /sbin/audio
start /sbin/usb-audio
start /sbin/agentd
start /sbin/speech
